Subject: [PATCH 02302/11362] [conductor] In-process docs for PHASE C (ARC
 NORTH STAR; shallow tail) -- adapter-free graph-explore DISCOVERY SWEEP over
 the remaining unsolved SHALLOW-tail games + reverse-engineer tn36's ACTION6
 click-payload schema. The 2026-06-17 sweep cracked 7 games adapter-free
 (cd82/sp80/su15/tu93 + cn04/m0r0/sk48 via E1 salience+mask); 13 games remain
 unsolved. EXCLUDE the deep-tail E3 games (ar25/ka59/tr87/ft09 -- exp4327-4329
 own those) and sc25 (provisional). SWEEP the shallow-tail candidates
 (bp35/dc22/g50t/lf52/re86/s5i5/sb26/vc33) with graph_explore_solve_v2/v3
 (arXiv:2512.24156: salience-prioritized state-transition graph, shortest-path
 to untested state-action pairs) at the 12k DISCOVERY budget (per the budget
 finding: 12k is load-bearing for first-level discovery; do NOT inflate the
 +1-advance budget). RE tn36's ACTION6 data schema (it raises KeyError 'x' --
 its click payload is NOT {{x,y}}; wrap clicks in tn36's expected payload
 before the explorer can advance it). CAPTURE + reproduction-gate any new L1
 solves (arc_solver_kit.reproduce). Update ops/arc_solve_registry.yaml.
 Monotonic +1+: report reproducible_total_levels (>= the current 13, ideally
 more) + games_advanced. verifier_is_oracle=true (execution-grounded). An
 honest no-advance WITH exploration_actions_used>0 per game is COMPLETE and
 informs the next pick; capture the per-game dead-ends. NO TRM training; NO
 leaderboard submission.

Co-Authored-By: Codex CLI <noreply@openai.com>
